---
import GranolaSimulator from "./react/GranolaSimulator";
// The granola sheet plus the supermarket research behind the starter mixes.
// Historical research only. Live economics are calculated in granola.ts.
const ingredients = [
  { name: "Oats", shelf: "Bokomo Morning Oats · Rs 82 / 500 g", note: "Winners listing; test flake size and crunch in the bake.", url: "https://www.winners.mu/cereales" },
  { name: "Almonds", shelf: "Seeberger almonds · Rs 365 / 200 g", note: "Winners listing; premium branded supermarket pack.", url: "https://www.winners.mu/seeberger-almonds-200g" },
  { name: "Raisins", shelf: "Melissa raisins · Rs 175 / 250 g", note: "Winners listing; add after baking.", url: "https://www.winners.mu/melissa--raisin-sec-250g" },
  { name: "Honey", shelf: "Allowance · Rs 250 / 500 g", note: "Historical anchor: Tropic Rs 193 regular price in Intermart’s Nov–Dec 2025 brochure. Budget raised to Rs 250; current shelf price unverified.", url: "https://intermartmauritius.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/INTERMART-BROCHURE-FROM-25-NOV-TO-15-DEC-2025.pdf" },
  { name: "Sunflower oil", shelf: "Sunlife sunflower oil · Rs 96 / litre", note: "Winners listing; 18 g ≈ 19.6 ml, assuming 0.92 g/ml.", url: "https://www.winners.mu/category/products?categoryId=151&pagenumber=4" },
  { name: "Cinnamon + salt", shelf: "Allowance · Rs 2 per pack", note: "Small seasoning allowance; replace with actual quantities and receipt prices.", url: null },
];
---
<section class="[&_a]:text-fg [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-[0.2em]" aria-label="Granola sheet and sources">
  <GranolaSimulator client:load />
  <details class="[&>p]:my-5 [&>p]:max-w-[85ch] [&>p]:leading-[1.75] [&>p]:text-fg-muted">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer border-t border-line py-6 font-display text-[1.6rem] text-fg">Ingredient research &amp; sources <span class="mt-2 block font-mono text-[0.65rem] text-fg-muted">Historical supermarket snapshot · 14 September 2026</span></summary>
    <p>These listings informed the starter mixes. They are not live quotes or confirmed Tamarin stock. Update the source, shelf quantity and price in the editor when you get a supplier quote. Honey, seasoning, packaging and operating expenses include planning allowances.</p>
    <div class="my-6 max-w-full overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Ingredient supermarket sources">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[620px] border-collapse text-left text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.5] [&_:is(th,td)]:border-b [&_:is(th,td)]:border-line [&_:is(th,td)]:p-4 [&_:is(th,td)]:align-top"><caption class="pb-[0.8rem] text-left text-[0.8rem] text-fg-muted">Original source notes · current costs come from your draft above</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-accent-text">Ingredient</th><th scope="col" class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-accent-text">Retail reference</th><th scope="col" class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-accent-text">What to check</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{ingredients.map(item=><tr><th scope="row" class="text-fg">{item.name}</th><td class="text-fg-muted">{item.url?<a href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{item.shelf} ↗</a>:item.shelf}</td><td class="text-fg-muted">{item.note}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Alternative oat sources from the same research: <a href="https://www.scotthomedelivery.mu/products/jungle-cooking-oats-1kg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Scott / Jungle rolled oats</a> and <a href="https://mantrafoods.mu/collections/cereals-breakfast-foods" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Mantra / organic oats</a>. Enter the quoted size, price, discount and allocated freight to compare them in your recipe.</p>
    <p>Measure the cooled yield and everyone's paid time, including shopping, oven supervision, packing and cleaning. Two people working for one hour count as two paid hours. The loaded hourly rate is a planning input; replace it with the full cost of your actual employment arrangement.</p>
    <p>The monthly result covers the operating costs entered in the draft. Add rent, insurance or other recurring expenses as cost rows when applicable. Setup equipment, kitchen alterations, testing, tax and any club contribution need separate amounts before deciding on a launch budget. Buying whole supplier packs also requires cash for ingredients left in inventory.</p>
    <p>Cost a measured batch, take paid orders, and record repeat purchases. A price change does not tell us how demand will change: update volume and sell-through using what customers actually do.</p>
  </details>
</section>
